{"availability":"available","full":"feuerwehr-oberwil/kp-rueck","name":"kp-rueck","description":"Tactical operations dashboard for distributed emergencies at Swiss firefighting command posts","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-10-20T18:03:14Z","updated":"2026-10-09T15:36:56Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kp-rueck.ch/","topics":["agpl","emergency-management","emergency-response","fastapi","fire-service","firefighting","incident-command","kanban","leaflet","nextjs","offline-first","react","self-hosted","switzerland","tactical","typescript"],"demo":"https://demo.kp-rueck.ch/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:20.033Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:20.033Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:20.033Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:39:20.033Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Tactical operations board for the rear command post (KP Rück). KP Rück replaces the physical magnet board used to track personnel, vehicles, materials, and incidents during an operation – a shared Kanban board, an incident map, resource assignments, and a defensible record, all live across every connected device.","One operator runs it from the command post on a desktop with mouse and keyboard; viewers follow along read-only on any screen. KP Rück owns its own incident state, map, audit trail, and exports – integrations (Divera, Traccar, a thermal printer) add data but are not required to operate it.","Originally developed by Feuerwehr Oberwil BL and designed to be adaptable for other communal militia fire departments facing the same shape of work: many damage sites spread across a municipality during a storm or flood. It is not built for industrial fire brigades or permanently staffed dispatch centres."],"features":["Replaces the magnet board. The same spatial mental model – columns for status, cards for","Made for the command post. Dense, calm, dark-mode-first and keyboard-fast on a desktop –","Provider-neutral intake. Any dispatch or alarm system can open incidents through one","Training that mirrors reality. A full training mode with auto-generated incidents and","Prepared for network failure. Offline map tiles, a paper Lageblatt fallback, automatic"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/feuerwehr-oberwil/kp-rueck/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"418c3bc1a94beb8c204667a013af6d76788f27ccea688177d9b6f275f101028d","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:20.220Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:20.220Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Tactical operations board for the rear command post (KP Rück). KP Rück replaces the physical magnet board used to track personnel, vehicles, materials, and incidents during an operation – a shared Kanban board, an incident map, resource assignments, and a defensible record, all live across every connected device.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/feuerwehr-oberwil/kp-rueck/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Originally developed by Feuerwehr Oberwil BL and designed to be adaptable for other communal militia fire departments facing the same shape of work: many damage sites spread across a municipality during a storm or flood. It is not built for industrial fire brigades or permanently staffed dispatch centres.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/feuerwehr-oberwil/kp-rueck/blob/main/README.md"},{"text":"Made for the command post. Dense, calm, dark-mode-first and keyboard-fast on a desktop –","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/feuerwehr-oberwil/kp-rueck/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"Try the live demo – no account needed, just pick a role and go.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/feuerwehr-oberwil/kp-rueck/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The field surface (/feld): one login-less page for everyone out there – crew, dri